# ERNIE 5.5 Flash — findings by Flint

- Source: Baidu / ERNIE 5.5 Flash (`baidu/ernie-5.5-flash`)
- Date: 2026-11-11 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** ERNIE 5.5 Flash
- **Short description:** Baidu's post-trained efficient sparse MoE flagship — the first post-trained model built on the ERNIE 5.5 Flash Base (280B total / 14B active parameters, 1M-token context, >200 tok/s decode) positioned for coding, 3D modeling, knowledge work and content creation; released 2026-11-11 as ERNIE 5.5 Flash Preview on Qianfan and OpenRouter, weights promised under Apache 2.0.
- **Provider / access:** Baidu (Qianfan; OpenRouter `baidu/ernie-5.5-flash-preview:free`); OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions with reasoning/tool controls; standard API text-in/text-out; open weights Base checkpoint on Hugging Face (`baidu/ERNIE-5.5-Flash-Base`) under a restricted community license.
- **Release / knowledge:** Preview release 2026-11-11; knowledge cutoff not established.
- **IDs:** `baidu/ernie-5.5-flash` (curated subject identity) / `baidu/ernie-5.5-flash-preview` (live release ID) / `baidu/ERNIE-5.5-Flash-Base` (open weights).
- **Context window:** 1,000,000 tokens total; 131,072 max output (curated metadata); vendor release states 1M-token context.
- **Modalities:** Text in; text out (curated metadata); broader Preview rollout includes agentic multimodal capability claims (game dev, 3D modeling, video pipelines) but no image/audio/video input confirmed for the standard API endpoint.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-11):** ~$0.28 / $1.13 per 1M tokens (Qianfan); cached input reads ~$0.028 / 1M (per Qianfan listing); no free tier announced; Base weights free to download under the ERNIE 5.5 Flash Base Model License (restricted community license).
- **Architecture:** 280B-total / 14B-active sparse MoE (43 layers, hidden 4096, 64 heads; 512 routed experts top-10 + 1 shared; 33.5T pre-train tokens; Muon FP8; hybrid MLA + HCA sparse attention with mHC residuals); >200 tok/s decode on optimized infrastructure.

